        "username": "schadkehnfreude",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/schadkehnfreude/{size}/2357_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-11-22T18:16:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"broccoli\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/48/1861_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> broccoli:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In my games, I used Savage Mana and put all the relics under it. &nbsp;Once that's done…kinda easy.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's a cool trick I hadn't thought of! &nbsp;Just to clarify from a rules POV - For purposes of PW Fanatic's unlock, destroying Savage Mana with End of Days explicity destroys the targets underneath per EoDay's card text. &nbsp;But, if she destroys Savage Mana with Consecrated Ground, does that cause <strong>her</strong> to then also destroy the targets stuffed underneath Haka's belly as well?</p>",
