      {
        "id": 184722,
        "name": "jorgenp",
        "username": "jorgenp",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/958977/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-11-23T12:56:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In those cases the unlocks are only looking for targets that entered the trash and doesn't care who did it. &nbsp;In this situation Fanatic has to specifically destroy the targets and if they are under Savage Mana she isn't destroying them. &nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Note, though, that End of Days is attributed to her.&nbsp; When End of Days triggers, it destroys all cards on the field in the order of your choosing.&nbsp; The cards below Savage Mana count as targets (as they do for all effects which can target Environment cards).&nbsp; Thus, provided you choose to destroy the cards under Savage Mana before you destroy Savage Mana, then that destruction will be attributed to Fanatic, as the player of End of Days.</p>",
        "post_number": 136,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:10:06.938Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
